 # Decorators & Generators ⚡

these two things looked scary
but they're actually pretty clean

---

## Decorators
basically a function inside a function
used to add extra behaviour

def my_decorator(func):
    def wrapper():
        print("before function")
        func()
        print("after function")
    return wrapper

@my_decorator
def say_hello():
    print("hello!")

say_hello()
# before function
# hello!
# after function

## real world use:
→ timing functions
→ login required checks
→ logging

---

## Generators
like a list but generates
one value at a time
saves memory!

def count_up(n):
    for i in range(n):
        yield i  # yield not return!

gen = count_up(5)
print(next(gen))  # 0
print(next(gen))  # 1
print(next(gen))  # 2

## why generators?
→ don't load everything in memory
→ great for large data
→ used a lot in AI/ML pipelines

## key difference
return → gives value, stops function
yield  → gives value, pauses function
